 of dealing with this is  to reduce the minimum term that I impose  by the total amount of time that you  have spent in custody for your attack on  Jackie  and by that I mean  from you being remanded in custody  before the first trial to serving part  of the notional determinate sentence it  also includes the time after the  specified period of nine years when the  parole board did not consider you safe  to be released and it also includes the  two periods when you were recalled to  custody after you had been released on  license  the total period of your incarceration  uh related to the of a fence on Jackie  as at today's date is agreed at 11 year  eight sorry 18 years 11 months and 25  days  so from a starting point of 30  the aggravating factors of such cruel  Behavior towards Jackie so lacking  inhumanity for the reasons I've set out  would take the Tariff to 35 and a half  years  but you are entitled to some allowance  for your limited mitigation your lack of  intention to kill the progress such as  it is that you have made in prison and  more minimally still the passage of time  I've also taken account of your sense of  disappointment that after having been  released in 2019 because of Jack's death  you are now facing a second long period  of imprisonment based on exactly the  same facts  those mitigating factors would entitle  you to a total deduction of 18 months  from the minimum period appropriate for  your offense  which would therefore take it to 34  years  taking into account the period of 18  years 11 months and 25 days I therefore  set the minimum term at 15 years and  five days  in other words if I can put it more  simply  your murder of Jackie justifies a total  minimum term of imprisonment of 34 years  in your life sentence but because you  have already served nearly 19 years for  causing the Grievous bodily harm that  she so bravely endured for 21 years the  term I now impose of 15 years and five  days is the balance that would bring the  local minimum term to 34 years  it's important that you and everyone  concerned with this case should  understand what this means  the minimum term is not a fixed term  after which you will automatically be  released  it is the term that must be served  before the parole board can undertake  their first review of the case  they will then review the risk that you  present at that stage and will consider  whether you can properly be released  from custody subject to license and if  so what the terms of that license should  be  if you are released you will be subject  to license for the rest of your life  if for any reason your license is  revoked you'll be recalled to prison to  continue to serve your life sentence in  custody  it follows that unless and until the  parole board consider that your release  is appropriate  you will remain in custody  finally  I'm required to State an open court that  a surcharge of 190 pounds imposed by  section 42 of the sentencing act 2020  applies in your case and perhaps finally  finally the last word should go to the  family of Jackie for all that they have  endured and the way they have stood by  her and cared for her over this long and  difficult period  and finally finally finally can I thank  all the lawyers in this case who've  helped with this difficult and  distressing  case  thank you very much indeed
 

